course: dictionary
lesson: 3789
title: Footrest and the parts of a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A footrest is something you rest your feet on. The word has two smaller words inside it, foot and rest, and together they give the meaning: a rest for your feet.
explain: «When you sit, your back should be supported and your feet flat on the floor or a footrest.» The word "or" tells you a footrest is another place for your feet, instead of the floor. Your feet are flat and resting, not dangling.
explain: Splitting a word into smaller parts is a useful trick. Foot plus rest makes footrest, just as headrest and armrest are built from smaller words. Check your guess by swapping it into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you are probably right.
fact: A footrest is something you rest your feet on while sitting.
fact: A footrest can be a small bar on a chair or a separate stool.
fact: Bikes, motorbikes, wheelchairs and pushchairs can have footrests where the feet go.
fact: Footrest is a compound word: two smaller words, foot and rest, joined together.
fact: Good posture means your back is supported and your feet are flat, often on a footrest when your feet do not reach the floor.
exercise: «Her feet did not reach the floor, so she put them on the footrest.» What is a footrest? | A type of shoe | A bed for a cat | A kind of rain | *Something you rest your feet on
exercise: Look at this sentence: «The bike has a footrest on each side.» Find and copy the word made of two smaller words joined together. | side | each | *footrest | bike
exercise: Ravi sits in his wheelchair. Which part helps him rest his feet? | A ceiling light | A pencil case | A rucksack | *A footrest
test: Which is the best way to check the meaning of footrest in a sentence? | *Swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense | Ask someone to say it for you | Count the letters in the word | Skip the sentence and forget it
test: «A motorbike has footrests where the rider's feet go.» Where do the rider's feet go? | Inside the helmet | *On the footrests | On the seat cover | On the handlebars
exam: Which two smaller words make up footrest? | hand and rest | *foot and rest | foot and stool | foot and wheel
